repository-code: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/llama-roofline"
url: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/llama-roofline"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21842493"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21842493"
    description: "Concept DOI, always resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22131998"
    description: "DOI for version v0.2.0"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that measures whether llama.cpp token generation on a given
  machine is limited by memory bandwidth. It measures the machine's sustainable
  memory-read bandwidth with a portable microbenchmark, benchmarks the user's own
  GGUF models with llama-bench across a thread sweep, fits the decode roofline
  tok/s = BW_eff / model_bytes, and reports the resulting bandwidth utilisation
  together with the optimal quantization and thread configuration. It also answers
  which quantization format to run on the local CPU core, from a shipped matrix of
  controlled measurements across three microarchitectures that includes energy and
  perplexity, stating its evidence basis per core and declining to guess on silicon
  it has no measurement for.
keywords:
  - llama.cpp
  - large language models
  - roofline model
  - memory bandwidth
  - quantization
  - edge inference
